  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The SEN136B5B has the same three pins (GND, 5V, SIG) as the catalogue's Ping))) sensor, so type ping-sensor is used.",
   "In the image the breadboard half that holds the sensor is labelled rows j-f. The catalogue names that half bank 'b' (rows f-j). The sensor pins GND, 5V and SIG are in columns 9, 10 and 11 at row j. Each wire ends in the same column at row f, so it shares a strip with its sensor pin.",
   "Arduino GND is wired to the GND header pin beside AREF, which is named GND.1. The tutorial text and schematic show only one GND connection.",
   "The schematic and the text agree with the image: 5V to 5V, GND to GND, SIG to digital pin 7. No resistor is needed."
  ]
 },
